※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4937 LANG_SPREAD_NOT_HERE

※ `⁂` in a collection written out is where a macro spreads what it holds, and
※ expansion has done that before anything is checked.  One the program wrote
※ itself spreads nothing a macro holds: a tuple is spread into a call or a
※ tuple, and written into a collection its members are written out.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let t: 〈u8, u8〉 = 〈1u8, 2u8〉
    let l: [u8] = [⁂t]
    if #l = 2: 0u6 else: 1u6
